## The 5 Vintage Styles

Cushion cut works with 5 distinct setting aesthetics on a men's band. Each one maps to a different historical design era. Each one changes what the ring signals to the room.

---

### Style 1 — Art Deco Geometric

**The look:** Precision grooves on the shank, geometric symmetry, the cushion stone floating in a clean seat. This is the 1920s aesthetic — structured, angular, modern for its era.

**The setting:** [Tapered Grooved Solitaire](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-tapered-grooved-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-147386?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). The grooved shank echoes the cushion's facet pattern. The taper from band to head draws the eye to the stone.

**The pairing:** [Tapered Grooved Solitaire, 14k White Gold — $1,000](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-tapered-grooved-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-147386?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [1ct GIA G-VS1 cushion — $1,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/23740863?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$2,891 total**. Cheapest complete ring in this guide with a natural GIA stone.

→ Art Deco pick: [Tapered Grooved Solitaire, 14k Yellow Gold — $1,000](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-tapered-grooved-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-item-147406?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [1ct GIA G-VS1 — $1,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/23740863?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Yellow gold amplifies the cushion's warm glow. Total: $2,891.

---

### Style 2 — Edwardian Ridged

**The look:** Horizontal ridges running the length of the shank. Clean, deliberate, masculine. The Edwardian era (1901–1910) valued precision detail on wide bands. The ridged shank carries that DNA.

**The setting:** [Ridged Solitaire](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-ridged-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-147412?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). The parallel ridges frame the cushion's soft profile. Where the cushion is curved, the band is linear. The contrast is what makes it work.

**The pairing:** [Ridged Solitaire, 14k White Gold — $1,224](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-ridged-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-147412?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [1ct GIA G-VS1 cushion — $1,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/23740863?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$3,115 total**. This is the entry-level pick for anyone who wants a GIA natural on a detailed band.

→ Edwardian pick: [Ridged Solitaire, Platinum — $2,096](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-ridged-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-147418?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [1ct GIA G-VS1 — $1,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/23740863?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Platinum ridges age better than gold — no replating. Total: $3,987.

---

### Style 3 — Victorian Solitaire

**The look:** Clean architectural shank, the stone as the sole focal point. Victorian solitaires were simple, commanding, and built for permanence. The cushion's heritage silhouette fits this aesthetic better than any modern cut.

**The setting:** [Structured Solitaire](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-structured-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-147399?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Heavy architectural shank. Wide seat that holds the cushion flat. The stone is the entire story.

**The pairing:** [Structured Solitaire, 14k White Gold — $1,732](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-structured-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-147399?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [1ct GIA G-VS1 cushion — $1,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/23740863?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$3,623 total**. This is the best-value pick. The architectural shank suits the cushion's soft geometry better than any other setting in this guide.

→ Victorian upgrade: [Structured Solitaire, Platinum — $2,424](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-structured-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-147405?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [1ct GIA G-VS1 — $1,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/23740863?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Platinum structured shank — the 20-year ring. Total: $4,315.

---

### Style 4 — Georgian Hammered

**The look:** Hand-hammered surface texture across the entire shank. Georgian jewelry (pre-1840) was made by hand. The hammered finish is the closest modern equivalent to that era's surface work. Against a cushion's smooth polished facets, it creates a raw vs refined contrast.

**The setting:** [Nugget Ring](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-nugget-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-146894?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Hammered organic texture across the full shank. The most distinctive setting in this guide. It signals history without looking costume.

**The pairing:** [Nugget Ring, 14k White Gold — $1,740](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-nugget-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-146894?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [1ct GIA G-VS1 cushion — $1,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/23740863?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$3,631 total**. If the structured settings feel too clean, this is your alternative.

→ Georgian upgrade: [Nugget Ring, Platinum — $2,652](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-nugget-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-146900?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [1ct GIA G-VS1 — $1,891](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/23740863?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Platinum hammered — maximum weight and presence. Total: $4,543.

---

### Style 5 — Modern Vintage

**The look:** Clean architectural setting, larger lab-grown cushion, same heritage silhouette at a fraction of the natural cost. The modern vintage approach gets you a 1.5ct+ cushion face-up for under $3,500. No compromise on the vintage aesthetic — the cushion shape reads the same at 1ct and 1.5ct.

**The pairing:** [Structured Solitaire, 14k White Gold — $1,732](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-structured-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-147399?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [1.5ct IGI E-VVS2 lab cushion — $1,422](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28961887?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$3,154 total**. A 6.3mm × 6.3mm face-up lab cushion on an architectural men's band. A natural 1.5ct cushion at this quality starts at $6,000+.

→ Modern Vintage upgrade: [Structured Solitaire, 14k White Gold — $1,732](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/mens-structured-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-147399?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [2ct IGI D-VVS1 lab cushion — $2,606](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28884982?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). A 7.0mm × 7.0mm cushion on a 7mm band — 100% coverage. Total: $4,338.

