## Expert Summary

**Farzana Hasan, diamond expert** | [About Farzana](/about-farzana/)

Cushion cut is the stone I recommend when a man wants something that looks like it has a history. The rounded corners carry a 19th-century profile that no modern cut can replicate. It sits flat on a wide band. Standard prongs grip it correctly. There is no corner risk to manage.

The price argument is compelling. A certified GIA natural cushion at 1ct starts at $1,891. That is 41% less than a round at the same certification. The savings are real and consistent. Use that gap to put the stone on a platinum Ridged Solitaire. You'll still come in under $4,000.

For lab-grown, the 1.5ct IGI cushion at $1,422 is the strongest value in this guide. That's a 6.3mm × 6.3mm face-up on a 7mm band — 90% coverage. Five years ago this price point didn't exist.

Pick your style era first. Then match the setting. Then add the cushion stone at checkout.

Entry point: [$2,891](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?Genders=men&ShapeID=Cushion&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for a GIA-certified 1ct cushion on a men's tapered grooved solitaire. Lab 1.5ct option: [$3,154](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28961887?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

